WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.850
KOTOBUKI of the Setting Sun

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.850
Quit mucking around!

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.130
Think of every second you waste as victory
getting a hundred times further out of reach!

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:07.750
Roger!

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.750
These are the last of our back up fighters,
so don't you go getting shot down!

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.000
It's unfortunate that things 
had to work out this way.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:14.790
Is it?

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.000
Loulou! There's one last 
thing I want to say to you!

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.380
First Officer.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.380
Thank you for your service.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.080
I hope you will help us see 
this through to the end.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.750
Oh no, yeah, thanks...

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:28.790
I'll be here!

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.340
What are you looking at?

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.420
It's those long pauses of his that
make things so uncomfortable, yes?

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.750
You think so? I see them as 
more of one of his strengths.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.890
You truly are a wicked woman.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.250
How rude.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.420
You do this all hands off then, and let
your little minions dance around for you, don't you?

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:52.880
I simply prefer to leave 
the dancing to the dancers.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:58.920
If I were as clever as you, perhaps Gadoll
would have faced a different fate.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.330
Now now Julia, let's not go talking
as if this is over already.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.750
True. We still have work to do.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.290
Whether this is a battle for
new beginnings or a new end, well...

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.540
Well, whatever happens, happens!

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.800
Don't you so much as flinch! 
We fight to the bitter end!

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.390
I don't care if you're the 
last man standing, you fight!

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:04.580
Naomi squadron, make your approach
from your eight o'clock.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.170
Your target is Isao Tower.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.670
What? We're under attack?
They don't even stand a chance. Why even bother?

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.250
They foolishly believe that where
there's a will, there's a way.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.290
I wish they wouldn't rush 
to their deaths like this.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.830
If they would just submit and obey I would give them
more work than they could ever hope for!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:33.590
I have given the evacuation orders for
the civilians and secured their safety.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:34.750
Master Isao, you should also hurry and--

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.170
Boy I sure do wanna get out there and fight!

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.670
Repairs will still take some time.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.710
Not much we can do about that, huh?
Guess we just stall for time, then?

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.420
Good grief.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:51.250
I'm normally much more 
suited for nonmanual labor!

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:06.500
Oh my! Anti-air towers?! We 
didn't have those in Shouto.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.040
Ikesuka sure is something else!

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.330
Air combat sure is fun, huh!

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.340
Can't beat the rush you get
shooting down another plane.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.000
Getting shot down sure does stink, though.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:26.670
Why do these people even bother fighting
a fight they know they can't win?

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.710
Are they stupid, or just obsessed?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.190
Isao's forces don't seem to have spotted
the KOTOBUKI Corps yet.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.250
Kylie, Chika, you two move in from
the Sugar Crystal District.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.130
Emma and Kate, you push right through
the Snuggy-wuggy Swamp.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:38.130
Zara and I will head straight for Isao Tower.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.540
Reona, what do you say the 
two of us just run away.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.630
Why not just leave all of this behind and
live out a new life somewhere far away?

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.170
Somewhere you can do whatever
it is you really want to do.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.080
That's out of the question.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.880
We have a duty here.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:53.790
We have no such thing.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.960
There's not a single thing out here
we have any obligation to do.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.460
So why don't you share some of
that burden you carry with me, sometimes?

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:02.680
I want to stay with you.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:04.470
Zara-

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.170
Take a look at that! The sky's all weird!

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:09.460
It's a new hole.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:10.600
What? Already?!

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.460
That's a little sooner than I 
expected, and a bit off course.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.960
I figured it'd be at least a short ways out.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.080
But it's right above them.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:17.830
Which means?

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:20.210
Isao has definitely noticed.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.580
We have a report from the Shouto Squadron.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:24.210
An additional thirty enemy 
aircraft spotted taking off.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.380
Assume these fighters are headed out
to deal with the KOTOBUKI Corps.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:27.580
Busted, huh?

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.380
Just how badly do they want 
this thing for themselves?

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.660
Less than five minutes until contact.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.830
We don't stand a chance 
against numbers like that.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.330
Girls, I don't suppose any 
of you have any suggestions?

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.960
Two heads are better than one.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:38.880
What's that supposed to mean?

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.460
It means if we all think together,
we might come up with a better plan.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.090
Well, six heads must be way better than one,
so get ready for the best plan of all!

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.880
How about we focus on low, narrow spaces?

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.880
So we take the fight straight into the city?

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:51.430
Mhmm!

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.980
Our Hayabusas' strength is in their handling.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.730
They're perfect for taking out 
those anti-air towers, too.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:00.330
It's time we show these fiends
that speed is not everything.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.290
All right, then we take 
the fight into the city!

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.920
The city, huh...

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.920
Yup, and we show them 
everything we're made of.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:07.540
Got it!

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.040
Zara.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.080
Yeah?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.460
You think things will be okay
without me pulling all the strings?

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:18.210
Of course! Why would we even be a team at all
if any of us could do this all on our own?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.540
Thanks.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:23.880
Okay girls, are you ready?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.260
Yee-up!

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:24.670
Of course.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:25.550
Absolutely!

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:26.300
I'm ready!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.300
Let's do this!

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.170
All right!

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.760
Fly high, KOTOBUKI Flight Corps!

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.630
Yes, ma’am!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:07.630
Flying straight down New Brotherhood Avenue
here is the shortest route to the tower.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.750
All blocked off, is it? I 
suppose we might have guessed.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.920
We can still turn and head 
straight up Trust Boulevard

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:14.960
We move on our three, then!

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:43.090
Kate!

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:52.920
This is Kate.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:55.130
The rockets on that unidentified 
craft appear to be

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:57.370
equipped with a proximity fuze. Stay alert.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.210
What should we do?

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:00.790
You can't just evade, you need to circumvent them with
sweeping turns. Big ones!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:01.420
Big ones?

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.330
Huge ones!

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:10.370
Proximity fuze missiles don't need to land hits
because they detonate

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.250
in proximity of their targets.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:13.830
But how can they tell when they're close?

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:14.880
Via radar.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.750
This is going to be a problem. 
We need to split up!

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.300
Emma, you follow Reona and I.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.500
As you wish.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.170
This is Kate. I've been 
downed on Hope Boulevard.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.830
Copy that. We're on our way 
to get you as we speak.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:50.670
Would she even shed a tear if I died?

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.290
To think the day would come when
I would need to take up arms again.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:57.040
I've heard that line more than once before.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.500
Oh no, but this truly was an unexpected turn!

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.290
Let's just hope it's the last.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.920
Though it may be the last 
in more ways than one...

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.920
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.250
Loulou...

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.830
What the heck! Don't just barge in like that!

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:14.880
I'm going, I'm going!

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.000
No! Don't look!

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:25.270
People like you who incite the innocent and seek


00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:29.070
to steal away what little 
we have for yourselves...

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.570
Don't deserve to fly!

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.670
Isao and the air pirates are pretty
much one in the same, huh?

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:39.790
I refuse to believe your twisted lies
of peace, happiness, and prosperity!

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.170
It went off-

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.380
--on that part sticking out there!

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:04.080
Let's get rid of this jerk!

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:04.830
Okay!

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:16.080
Here we go!

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:16.630
Yup!

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:28.290
Did we get him?

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:29.040
I think so!

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.420
We're real aces!

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.000
Chika!

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:33.590
They got me!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.630
Chika, are you all right?!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.090
I'm good! I'll wait for 
pickup here, you keep going!

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:40.260
Gah! We only had one of those 
lost little fighters there!

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.040
When that one came through a hole
had barely even opened.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.380
Don't think I don't know
you're here to block off that hole!

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:50.380
I'd say you're definitely 
better off with me around.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:51.960
I'm doing just fine right now without you.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.170
I don't mean now, I'm 
talking about our future!

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:56.630
Our what? Do you seriously think
you're gonna make it through this?

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.330
I was born to defend you.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:01.460
You're not making a damn bit of sense!

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:03.040
I'm proposing, okay? PROPOSING!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.370
I'm asking you to marry me!

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.330
Are you daydreaming over 
there or something, buddy?

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.670
How about you tell me about those dreams
of yours once we survive all this?

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.920
Kylie, get below the bridge!

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:32.170
Oh, right!

00:10:58.670 --> 00:10:59.680
I'll see you...

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.220
IN HELL!

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:27.210
I've been bested...

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:29.040
But I certainly feel better now!

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.380
It's time we settled our score!

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:36.790
You do not have what it takes.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.880
Don't you dare think you can even touch her!

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:44.960
Hatokichi!

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:45.960
It's time!

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:25.500
We only have two birds left!
What kind of monsters are you?!

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:27.920
They just shot one of their own down!

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:29.600
Don't worry, I'm on your side!

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.540
Now, my brother!

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:31.540
Roger that!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.140
Got 'em!

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:34.630
Brother!

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:35.750
They got me!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:36.670
I can see that!

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:40.210
Air pirates? What are they doing
fighting on Ikesuka's side?

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:41.000
Don't tell me...!

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.710
Now then, my friends, it's 
time to repay those debts!

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:47.580
Show Ikesuka and myself your thanks for all
the aid we have always smuggled your way!

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.000
Hey! Make sure you shoot 
some down for me, too!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:00.420
Impressive. But you are not 
quite as shrewd as I am.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.290
Ready the crane!

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:20.690
Ugh, you're the WORST!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:33.670
Anna, look!

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:34.160
The hole!

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.250
It's time.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:38.420
Farewell.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.170
HELL SPEED

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.460
You're time's just about up!

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:49.290
Master Isao.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:50.580
To our snack-time o'clock!

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:51.420
What is it?

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.210
It's an airship, stay alert!

00:14:53.210 --> 00:14:56.080
No ordinary airship moves 
at speeds like that.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:58.210
There it goes! You better make this worth it!

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.380
May the fortunes of war fall in your favor.

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:03.000
Closing up a hole that big will take
more than four tons of explosives.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.840
With that much it should blow in an instant.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.410
So that's it then? If they 
can't have it to themselves,

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.660
they aren't going to let anyone have it?!

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:11.920
What a stupid, dimwitted, idiotic idea!

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:16.220
I don't think so!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:48.750
You shoot down Ol' Sab, you attack Rahama,
and you still haven't had enough, you pighead?!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.170
I'm not gonna let you get away with this!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.540
Can you just leave me alone already?

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.460
As kind as I may be, you 
don't want to make me angry!

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:58.830
Kylie, you can't! You're gonna sink into
the deep, dark sea at this rate!

00:15:58.830 --> 00:15:59.930
Remember the line in See the Sea!

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:03.060
Anger and hatred only harden you like stone,

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.940
and once a stone sinks 
it never floats back up!

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:26.210
You don't fly a plane...

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.670
This is amazing, Ol' Sab!

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:45.330
Wait, what? What did he just say?

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:53.080
You don't fly a plane, they fly on their own.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:56.130
All a pilot needs to do is follow its lead.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.380
They fly...

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:05.120
On their own!

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:11.670
Okay! Time to finish you off!

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.580
If anger and hatred are what hold me down...

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:25.040
Then it's freedom that gives me wings!

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:28.860
Nobody, and none of this sky, belongs to you!

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:44.460
That's mine!

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.210
It's mine, all mine, and just for me!

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:48.790
It's going to be mine!

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:52.790
Mine to dominate! Mine to manage!
Mine to control! MINE!

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:55.330
It's not for anyone but me!

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:11.290
Gooo!!!

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:24.670
Hey you! Don't you dare just turn and run!

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:29.210
Do you have any idea how much time
and money we spent on you, you traitors?!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.960
Was this really the right thing to do?

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.000
Right how?

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.170
Blowing up the hole like that.

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:40.630
It might have brought us all sorts of stuff.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:42.720
And it might not have.

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:47.170
You're right, Ol' Sab.

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:48.960
I'm just gonna keep being me.

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:52.710
I did this all by my own hands,
of my own free will, after all!

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:58.040
Kylie are you there?! 
Come in! Come in already!

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:00.630
I'm starving.

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:01.750
You idiot!

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:02.420
What?!

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:05.290
I can't think of a more 
Kylie response than that!

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.540
Are you making fun of me?
After all the hard work I just did?

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.000
Only real idiots go around
telling people they worked hard!

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.580
Oh shut up, I only said it 'cause
it's not like anyone else was gonna.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:15.300
Fine, oh yeah, you were sooo amazing.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.210
Now, put some more feeling into it!

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:20.410
I can hardly hold back these 
tears of joy for how you

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:24.190
rid me of those bastards that plagued me so.

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:24.930
What's with the poetry?

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.420
You should have rolled a bit wider, huh?

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:28.830
I miscalculated.

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:31.790
I think I'll kick off my studies of
these holes again when we get back.

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:32.630
I'll help you.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:34.670
Maybe I'll just try and give her a call.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.630
Even though the Madame couldn't 
even sort things out?

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:39.250
It might work better hearing 
it straight from me!

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:40.130
Feel free, then.

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:43.710
Doesn't this all feel pretty refreshing?

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:44.380
How?

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:49.120
We're free to do whatever 
we want now, is what I mean.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.580
Same as it's always been.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:55.960
And same as it always will be, huh?

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.580
All right! I think it's time!

00:19:57.580 --> 00:19:58.540
Time for what?

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:02.260
For me to step out of this Raiden
and pass it on to the next generation.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.880
So I get to pilot the Raiden now?

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.350
In what world would that ever happen?

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.360
I'll make sure the First 
Ave theater, the bakery,

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:12.270
Takochu Park, and the 
cafeteria are all rebuilt!

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:14.000
Now then, where to go next!

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.500
Atazaki is a great place for a honeymoon.

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:17.880
Atazaki it is, then.

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:20.830
Well are we going to Atazaki, or not?

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:21.880
What?!

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:28.000
Do you take him for better, for worse, for richer,
for poorer, for dumb, for dumber?

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:30.080
Isn't he just gonna stick around anyway?

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:33.290
Of course I am, my lovely!

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:34.580
I'm going to buy myself a new handbag!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.170
And I'm going to buy some 
shiny, fancy sandals!

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.000
When we get back it's straight 
to repairs and tuning!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.880
As long as we've got the parts,
there's nothing we can't fix up.

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:41.920
You best be ready!

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:42.380
Roger!

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:42.930
As you wish!

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:46.250
The sheer number of problems
we'll have to deal with now is just dreadful.

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:49.000
Though maybe this will finally shake some
since into those fools in Gadoll.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.040
What a rough life.

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:52.130
And what do you plan on doing now?

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:53.380
The same as I always have.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:54.790
How, when you're flat out broke?

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:57.630
By doing what little I can, bit by bit.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:00.670
I think I'll start with a 
nice shower when I get home.

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:03.540
You never change.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:07.290
This is the Ouni Company, come in.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:10.660
It's a bright sunny day in Rahama today.
With winds blowing from the southeast at three khrill.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:13.540
Everyone is ready and 
waiting for your return.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:16.210
We're headed for Rahama now ourselves.

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:18.080
Fly safe, everyone.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:19.330
We'll see you in Rahama!

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:21.210
Oh, right!

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:21.920
What?

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:24.130
Does the name "KOTOBUKI" come
from the Yufang word?

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:26.640
Yeah, it means good fortune.

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:29.080
I heard it was more like 
a word of congratulations.

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:30.330
And for longevity.

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.850
Sounds like it means all 
sorts of great things.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.850
Sounds like a perfect match for us.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.790
I wonder if we'll still be 
flying when we're all old.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.080
We sure will!

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:48.000
Long ago, the world opened right up,
and lots rained down on us.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.420
Some good things. Some bad things.

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:52.880
Some lovely things. Some tarnished things.

00:21:53.380 --> 00:21:54.880
There was all sorts of stuff.

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:58.630
But now the world has closed up again.

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:04.670
And while we slowly lose many of the things
we have, we gain many more as well.

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:07.500
And we live on, latching on to what we have.

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:09.540
And we will continue living just this way.

00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:23.630
Ano sora o jiyuu ni kakenukete mitai to
I wanted to try and soar through that sky

00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:27.460
Hanasaki no kaze ni negai o noseta
So I wished upon the winds right before me

00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:31.380
Akogare ga keshiki o tsukutteiku
Our aspirations build us scenery

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:35.830
Ano toki no kaze wa genki kanaa
I wonder how that wind is now

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:44.170
Nan no tame ni tatakau no kana
Why do we fight, I wonder

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:48.210
Koko ni iru riyuu wa nan darou?
What is our purpose here?

00:22:48.210 --> 00:22:56.420
Toikaketa sora wa kotaenai kedo
I asked, but the skies do not answer

00:22:57.130 --> 00:23:04.080
Bokura wa tsubasa o motteiru
We all have wings

00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:08.790
Haruka kanata nageki no shuuchakuten
Far away at the end of all lament

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:13.040
Mitsuketa monogataritachi
The stories we found

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:20.830
Kono sora wa dare ni mo ubaenai
No one can steal these skies away

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:25.540
Boku wa kakeru nanimo kowakunai yo
We will soar unafraid of anything

00:23:25.540 --> 00:23:32.670
Shiawase nara koko ni aru yo
Because happiness is right here
